================================================================================================
PAIRED A/B:  design_resolution 4 vs 5,  same seeds, same r0=0.6
================================================================================================
  5 seeds x 20 epochs. Negative diff = res-5 better (lower energy).

  problem                  res4 mean   res5 mean  paired diff      sem   nefv   depth 4/5
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Heisenberg N=4             -5.9320     -5.9216       0.0103   0.0167     60       27/41
  Heisenberg N=6             -8.8623     -8.7944       0.0678   0.0602     60       45/62
  MaxCut N=4 (Opt=3.2)        0.0212      0.0248       0.0036   0.0054     20       27/41
  H2 Molecule                -1.8448     -1.8451      -0.0003   0.0014     40       19/22

================================================================================================
READING IT
================================================================================================
  A paired difference more negative than ~2 SEM is a real improvement
  and justifies re-tuning r0 for res-5 and rerunning the full suite.
  Anything inside the noise means v90's single-seed -5.5921 -> -5.8329
  was a draw of the dice, the aliasing fix helps the Hamiltonian-
  learning task it was built for and NOT VQE, and the suite stands.
  The depth column is the cost either way: res-5 spends more CNOTs on
  longer parity chains, and that is charged to nobody in the NEFV table.
